WEBVTT

NOTE The story: captions match the on-screen steps.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.274
Step 1 of 11. The question: does the mood online match life on the ground?.

2
00:00:06.274 --> 00:00:15.455
Step 2 of 11. Every dot is a Victorian suburb: size is tweet volume, colour is average tone.

3
00:00:15.455 --> 00:00:22.584
Step 3 of 11. The 2023 brief: harvest, store, analyse and compare with official data, on 8 vCPUs.

4
00:00:22.584 --> 00:00:26.011
Step 4 of 11. How it worked: scroll to follow a tweet through the original cloud system.

5
00:00:26.011 --> 00:00:31.714
Step 5 of 11. Harvest: MPI ranks split the 57 GB file; harvesters poll three Mastodon servers.

6
00:00:31.714 --> 00:00:37.382
Step 6 of 11. Score and store: VADER on a 1-9 scale, bulk-loaded into a three-node CouchDB cluster.

7
00:00:37.382 --> 00:00:42.853
Step 7 of 11. Summarise: MapReduce views keep a count, sum, min and max for every suburb.

8
00:00:42.853 --> 00:00:48.270
Step 8 of 11. Serve and compare: a Flask API joins the views with SUDO income and crime data.

9
00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:53.600
Step 9 of 11. Automate: Ansible and Docker Swarm on the Melbourne Research Cloud.

10
00:00:53.600 --> 00:01:01.701
Step 10 of 11. Four findings, recomputed from the recovered numbers.

11
00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:09.280
Step 11 of 11. The 2026 upgrade: intervals, spatial statistics and an optional, audited AI.
